* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13cmos5l-postlayout-pex-pvt (issue #30, Part of #16)
* POST-LAYOUT charge-pump DC characterisation -- the parasitic-annotated twin
* of ../../sg13cmos5l-cp-icp-trim/testbench/tb_cp_dc.sp.tmpl, kept
* line-for-line comparable to it so the only difference between the two
* campaigns' numbers is the extracted interconnect R/C.
*
* ../run_cp.sh substitutes @CORNER_MOS@ (cornerMOShv.lib), @TEMP@ (degC),
* @VDD@ (supply, V), @IREF@ (trim-code reference current, A), @UPV@/@DNV@
* (switch-input voltages) and @VOUTMAX@ over the SAME matrix that campaign
* ratified, and @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@ (ngspice's .lib parser does not expand
* environment variables, issue #44).
*
* The DUT is `pll_cp`, the subcircuit `klt extract --deck sg13cmos5l
* --parasitics --pdk ihp-sg13cmos5l` produced from the ROUTED GDS of layout
* record 20260830-204105-457cf5b: 20 devices, 18 nets, 80 parasitic resistors
* and 18 substrate + 88 coupling capacitors from klt's curated sg13cmos5l
* metal coefficients. `cp_inst.spice` is generated by ../run_cp.sh from the
* extracted subcircuit's own pin list, never transcribed by hand -- the
* extracted cell exposes all 18 nets as pins, so a hand-written port order
* would be a silent-miswire risk indistinguishable from a physical effect.
*
* This block is one of the three whose LVS the ../lvs-recheck/ pass confirms
* MATCHES its schematic (20/20 devices, 18/18 nets), so unlike the `pll_vco`
* arm, a deviation measured here cannot be attributed to an unverified
* layout-vs-schematic topology.

.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOShv.lib @CORNER_MOS@
.option scale=1 temp=@TEMP@

.include cp_pex.spice
.include cp_inst.spice

Vdd VDD 0 dc @VDD@

* The extracted netlist declares its own `.GLOBAL vsubs` and ties it to
* ground only through klt's 1e12-ohm DC tie. Every extracted net-to-ground
* parasitic capacitor returns to that node, so leaving it at 1e12 ohms would
* leave those capacitors driving a floating node and silently cancel most of
* the loading this record exists to measure. Held hard at 0 V, which is what
* the substrate physically is here.
Vsubs vsubs 0 dc 0

* --- the four trim-code reference currents, identical to the schematic arm
*     (P side sinks to 0, N side is sourced from 0 -- ngspice's Iname n+ n-) ---
Irefbp IBP 0 dc @IREF@
Irefcp ICP 0 dc @IREF@
Irefbn 0 IBN dc @IREF@
Irefcn 0 ICN dc @IREF@

Vup UP 0 dc @UPV@
Vdn DN 0 dc @DNV@
Vout VOUT 0 dc 1.65

* UPB/DNB are the schematic's INTERNAL inverter outputs, which the extracted
* cell surfaces as top-level pins. They are deliberately left driven by the
* cell's own `inv_hv` instances and NOT forced here -- forcing them would
* replace a real post-layout delay/level path with an ideal one and make the
* comparison against the schematic arm meaningless.

.control
dc Vout 0.15 @VOUTMAX@ 0.05
let icp = i(Vout)
wrdata sweep.dat icp
.endc
.end
